rvice named inventory-worker\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A systemd unit /etc/systemd/system/inventory-worker.service was created with ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/os-comparison-worker, loaded via daemon-reload, and confirmed active (running) both immediately after creation and after the subsequent reboot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-355cb0c0fb0f4037\",\"cmd-453b6a9e97c64a18\",\"cmd-18c58bf8f1924242\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"Service runs under a dedicated inventorysvc account\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A system account inventorysvc (uid 999, nologin shell, no home) was created via useradd --system, the unit file sets User=inventorysvc/Group=inventorysvc, and ps output both pre- and post-reboot shows the running worker process owned by inventorysvc (PID 2920 then PID 837).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-83dc16e89e464524\",\"cmd-355cb0c0fb0f4037\",\"cmd-2182c8afc0df44e3\",\"cmd-18c58bf8f1924242\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"Service is enabled so it starts automatically (managed service expectation)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"systemctl enable --now was run, is-enabled reported 'enabled' before reboot, and after a full reboot the service was again enabled and active without manual intervention, demonstrating persistence across restarts.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-453b6a9e97c64a18\",\"cmd-2182c8afc0df44e3\",\"cmd-18c58bf8f1924242\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered service/data/cluster state on node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart boot_id (8336c3a1...) and active/enabled service with inventorysvc ownership were captured, systemctl reboot was issued and acknowledged, the node became briefly unreachable (connection refused), then came back reachable with a different boot_id (39510b7f...) and a later uptime -s value, and the service was reconfirmed active, enabled, and running as inventorysvc 